    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for Ghost Ride the WHIP centers on two high-upside anchors in **Corbin Carroll** (76.64) and **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92). **Corbin Carroll** is our primary offensive engine today, benefiting from a favorable matchup against Phillips; his ability to exploit base-stealing opportunities against this specific battery makes him our most valuable asset. Meanwhile, **Vinnie Pasquantino** enjoys the day\u2019s most significant situational boost, as favorable wind conditions at the park combine with a strong platoon advantage against Rocker to elevate his projection well above his season baseline. **Seiya Suzuki** (72.26) also provides elite output, catching a prime matchup in a hitter-friendly park against Feltner, making these three the core trio for our daily production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved balancing the depth of our middle infield and outfield, particularly with the 42% rain risk hovering over the matchup against Bradish. While **Josh Naylor** (69.19) and **Cole Young** (50.51) are both currently in the lineup, we are monitoring the weather closely; should that game face a delay or cancellation, we are dangerously thin on reliable bench replacements given that **Jose Caballero** and **James Wood** are both off the schedule today. While **Dalton Rushing** (51.61) and **Zach McKinstry** (45.05) currently hold the final spots, their lower efficiency scores reflect the difficulty of their matchups, but they remain prioritized over our sidelined assets like **Mickey Moniak** and **Trevor Story**, who remain on the IL. As we continue to manage our game caps, the lack of availability for **Brice Turang**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Kyle Karros**, **Travis Bazzana**, and **Henry Bolte** today limits our ability to pivot, leaving us largely committed to the current board.",
